  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be the greatest integer less than or equals to <math><mi>x</mi></math>.&nbsp;Then, at which of the following point(s) the function <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msup><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></math> is discontinuous at all integers and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi></math> is continuous everywhere.</p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, so it&#39;s continuous.</p><p>At other integral points,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous.</p>"
  }
